Transformers Universe has been a long  time coming longer than you might have  hoped thanks to an executive decision to  rebuild the entire game in unity just a  year ago but it's a move that seems to  have paid off as free-to-play  browser-based MMOs go it looks the  business the game revolves around  classic pvp raid action albeit with a  tactical twist rather than just charging  in fists or rocket first into battle the  idea is to make use of each classes  unique abilities and work together as a  team to take down the opposition while  there's no character creator universe  does feature a whole set of new  transformers across 12 classes designed  exclusively for the game as well as some  familiar favorites + by mining Energon  from the environment you can tweak a  character skills to focus on a  particular area of expertise or create  more of an all-rounder all robots have a  particular key skill though tank  characters like the monster truck  transforming showdown focus on brute  strength with a shield sharing ability  letting them protect weaker members of  the team like snipers healers like  meltdown consists on the periphery of  the battle buffing melee characters like  frontline with a healing gun for  prolonged attacks ultimately it's how  well a team can strategize and use each  of those characters abilities together  that's the key to winning battles you  can use a few characters to distract a  group of opponents peeling one off from  the group and into a deadly ambush for  the tank full hide around a corner ready  to absorb a flurry of laser fire fling  it straight back edits creator if it all  gets a bit much you can transform into a  vehicle and hightail out of there taking  refuge near a healer to recharge or if  your character gets destroyed during  battle you can choose to redeploy it by  spending energy on on it or pick another  character from your stash and send it  into the fray sadly I didn't get a  chance to go hands-on with the game so  it's still up in the air as to how well  the combat and vehicles handle and  there's a question over how well  developer jagat handles all the  inevitable microtransactions especially  when there are so many collectible  trends  former Zhan offer but transformers  universe looks promising let's hope it  sees a release soon
 

